{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "def is_woodall(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given integer is a Woodall number, which is of the form n * 2^n - 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Woodall numbers satisfy the equation: number + 1 = n * 2^n\n    target_val = number + 1\n    n = 1\n    while True:\n        current_val = n * (2**n)\n        if current_val == target_val:\n            return True\n        if current_val > target_val:\n            # Since n * 2^n increases monotonically for n >= 1,\n            # if we've exceeded the target, no larger n will match.\n            return False\n        n += 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "def check(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    Returns True if the number satisfies the condition, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        # A negative number cannot be one less than twice a positive reversed number.\n        return False\n\n    original_number = number\n    reversed_num = 0\n    temp_num = number\n\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        digit = temp_num % 10\n        reversed_num = reversed_num * 10 + digit\n        temp_num //= 10\n\n    return original_number == (2 * reversed_num) - 1"}
