{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number, representing the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    It uses dynamic programming based on a recurrence relation involving binomial coefficients.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    def nCr(n_val, r_val):\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the binomial coefficient (n_val choose r_val).\n        \"\"\"\n        if r_val < 0 or r_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if r_val == 0 or r_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if r_val > n_val // 2:\n            r_val = n_val - r_val\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(r_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    bell = [0] * (n + 1)\n    bell[0] = 1\n\n    # B_i = sum_{k=0 to i-1} (i-1 choose k) * B_k\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        current_bell = 0\n        for k in range(i):\n            current_bell += nCr(i - 1, k) * bell[k]\n        bell[i] = current_bell\n        \n    return bell[n]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "def is_Monotonic(arr: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an array is monotonic (non-decreasing or non-increasing).\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_increasing = True\n    is_decreasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > arr[i-1]:\n            is_decreasing = False\n        elif arr[i] < arr[i-1]:\n            is_increasing = False\n        \n        # Optimization: If it's neither increasing nor decreasing, it's not monotonic\n        if not is_increasing and not is_decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return is_increasing or is_decreasing"}
