{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Eulerian number a(n, m) using an iterative approach.\n    Handles base cases and the recurrence relation a(n, m) = (n - m) * a(n-1, m-1) + (m + 1) * a(n-1, m).\n    \"\"\"\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a 2D array (list of lists) for dynamic programming\n    # dp[i][j] will store a(i, j)\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: a(0, 0) = 1\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i): # m can go up to n-1\n            # Recurrence relation: a(i, j) = (i - j) * a(i-1, j-1) + (j + 1) * a(i-1, j)\n            term1 = (i - j) * (dp[i-1][j-1] if j-1 >= 0 else 0)\n            term2 = (j + 1) * dp[i-1][j]\n            dp[i][j] = term1 + term2\n            \n    return dp[n][m]"}
