{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binaryString: str, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of rotations of a binary string that result in an odd integer.\n    An integer is considered odd if its binary representation ends with '1'.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Perform rotation by splitting and concatenating the string\n        rotated_string = binaryString[i:] + binaryString[:i]\n        # Check if the least significant bit (rightmost character) is '1'\n        if rotated_string[-1] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "solution": "def check_integer(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string represents an integer.\"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return False\n    \n    # Check for optional leading sign\n    start_index = 0\n    if s[0] == '+' or s[0] == '-':\n        start_index = 1\n    \n    # String must contain at least one digit after the optional sign\n    if start_index >= len(s):\n        return False\n\n    # Check if all remaining characters are digits\n    for i in range(start_index, len(s)):\n        if not '0' <= s[i] <= '9':\n            return False\n            \n    return True"}
