{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum difference between the number of 0s and number of 1s\n    in any sub-string of the given binary string using Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    def _kadane(nums):\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray, ensuring the result\n        is non-negative by resetting the current sum if it falls below zero.\n        \"\"\"\n        max_so_far = 0\n        current_max = 0\n        for x in nums:\n            current_max += x\n            if current_max < 0:\n                current_max = 0\n            if current_max > max_so_far:\n                max_so_far = current_max\n        return max_so_far\n\n    # Case 1: Maximize (count of 0s - count of 1s)\n    # Transform '0' to 1 and '1' to -1\n    transformed_s1 = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char == '0':\n            transformed_s1.append(1)\n        else: # char == '1'\n            transformed_s1.append(-1)\n    max_diff_zeros_minus_ones = _kadane(transformed_s1)\n\n    # Case 2: Maximize (count of 1s - count of 0s)\n    # Transform '0' to -1 and '1' to 1\n    transformed_s2 = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char == '0':\n            transformed_s2.append(-1)\n        else: # char == '1'\n            transformed_s2.append(1)\n    max_diff_ones_minus_zeros = _kadane(transformed_s2)\n\n    # The maximum absolute difference is the greater of the two maximums found.\n    return max(max_diff_zeros_minus_ones, max_diff_ones_minus_zeros)"}
