{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given element is a majority element in the sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate array length consistency and handle empty array.\n    if n != len(arr) or n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    def find_first(nums: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of the target using binary search.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(nums) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if nums[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1\n            elif nums[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    def find_last(nums: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of the target using binary search.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(nums) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if nums[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                low = mid + 1\n            elif nums[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    first_occurrence_idx = find_first(arr, element)\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_occurrence_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_occurrence_idx = find_last(arr, element)\n\n    # Calculate the total count of occurrences.\n    count = last_occurrence_idx - first_occurrence_idx + 1\n\n    # Check if the count exceeds n/2.\n    return count > n / 2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(num):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of set bits (binary digits with value 1) in a given number.\n    It uses Brian Kernighan's algorithm for efficient counting.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    while num > 0:\n        num &= (num - 1)  # Clears the least significant set bit\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
