{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Tuple\n\ndef convert(complex_number: complex) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Convert a complex number to polar coordinates.\n    Returns a tuple (r, theta) where r is magnitude and theta is angle in radians.\n    \"\"\"\n    if complex_number == 1:\n        return (1.0, 0.0)\n\n    real = complex_number.real\n    imag = complex_number.imag\n\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(real ** 2 + imag ** 2)\n    angle = math.atan2(imag, real)\n\n    return (magnitude, angle)"}
