{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers strictly less than n.\n    Uses the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n\n    for p in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[p]:\n            for multiple in range(p * p, n, p):\n                is_prime[multiple] = False\n\n    return sum(is_prime)"}
