{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into n sublists, distributing elements based on their original index modulo n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        # Based on the problem description and example, n is expected to be a positive integer.\n        # Returning an empty list of lists for n <= 0 handles this gracefully without errors.\n        return [[] for _ in range(max(0, n))]\n    \n    result = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for i, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        result[i % n].append(item)\n    return result"}
