{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "```python\ndef validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in 'number' is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    This function processes the input integer as a string to count digit occurrences.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        number = abs(number)  # Handle negative numbers by converting to positive\n\n    digit_counts = {}\n    for digit_char in str(number):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        digit_counts[digit] = digit_counts.get(digit, 0) + 1\n\n    for digit, count in digit_counts.items():\n        if count > digit:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/282", "solution": "def sub_list(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Subtract two numeric lists element-wise.\n    Raises ValueError if lengths differ, TypeError if elements are non-numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        val1 = list1[i]\n        val2 = list2[i]\n        if not isinstance(val1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(val2, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Non-numeric element at index {i}: {val1}, {val2}\")\n        result.append(val1 - val2)\n\n    return result"}
