{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in the given integer based on its current active bits.\n    For example, 10 (0b1010) becomes 14 (0b1110) by setting the bit at position 2.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Find the position of the most significant set bit.\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Iterate from the most significant bit's position downwards.\n    for k in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the k-th bit is unset (0).\n        if not (n & (1 << k)):\n            # If unset, set it and return the new integer.\n            return n | (1 << k)\n\n    # If all bits up to msb_pos are already set (e.g., n = 7 which is 0b111),\n    # return the original number as there's no unset bit in its active range.\n    return n"}
