{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "def convert_list_dictionary(ids, names, scores):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts three parallel lists into a list of nested dictionaries.\n    Each dictionary maps an ID to a sub-dictionary containing the corresponding name and score.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(ids)):\n        nested_dict = {ids[i]: {names[i]: scores[i]}}\n        result.append(nested_dict)\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum possible for a given integer n\n    using the recurrence f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _calculate_max_sum(k: int) -> int:\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        if k == 0:\n            return 0\n\n        # Calculate the sum of the parts using floor division\n        sum_of_parts = (\n            _calculate_max_sum(k // 2) +\n            _calculate_max_sum(k // 3) +\n            _calculate_max_sum(k // 4) +\n            _calculate_max_sum(k // 5)\n        )\n\n        # The result is the maximum of the sum of parts or k itself\n        result = max(sum_of_parts, k)\n\n        # Store the result in memoization table before returning\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _calculate_max_sum(n)"}
