{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "class Trapezium:\n    \"\"\"\n    Domain model representing a trapezium with two parallel bases.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, base1: float, base2: float):\n        self.base1 = base1\n        self.base2 = base2\n\n    def median(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculate the median (average of the two bases).\n        \"\"\"\n        return (self.base1 + self.base2) / 2.0\n\n\nclass MedianCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Service providing the median_trapezium function.\n    \"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def median_trapezium(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Compute the median of a trapezium given three numeric arguments.\n        The third argument is retained for API consistency but not used.\n        \"\"\"\n        trapezium = Trapezium(a, b)\n        return trapezium.median()\n\n\ndef median_trapezium(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper function exposed to consumers to calculate the median length of a trapezium.\n    The third argument `c` is not used in the calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    return MedianCalculator.median_trapezium(a, b, c)"}
