{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from index 0 to n inclusive.\n    The Perrin sequence is defined as P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2, and P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3) for k > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0 # Per instructions, no error checks, return 0 for negative n.\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 3\n\n    # Initialize the first three Perrin numbers\n    p_prev3 = 3  # P(0)\n    p_prev2 = 0  # P(1)\n    p_prev1 = 2  # P(2)\n\n    # Initialize total sum with P(0)\n    total_sum = p_prev3\n\n    if n == 1:\n        total_sum += p_prev2 # P(0) + P(1)\n        return total_sum\n    \n    # If n >= 2, add P(2)\n    total_sum += p_prev1 # P(0) + P(1) + P(2)\n\n    if n == 2:\n        return total_sum\n\n    # Calculate Perrin numbers and sum for n > 2\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        # Calculate P(i) using the recurrence relation P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3)\n        p_current = p_prev3 + p_prev2\n        total_sum += p_current\n\n        # Shift the previous values for the next iteration\n        p_prev3 = p_prev2\n        p_prev2 = p_prev1\n        p_prev1 = p_current\n    \n    return total_sum"}
