{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "def combinations_list(items_list):\n    # Initializes a list containing only an empty list, which is the starting point for all combinations.\n    all_combinations = [[]]\n\n    # Iterates through each element in the input list.\n    for item in items_list:\n        # Creates a temporary list to hold new combinations formed by including the current item.\n        newly_formed_combinations = []\n        # For each combination already found, create a new one by prepending the current item.\n        for existing_combination in all_combinations:\n            # Prepending 'item' ensures the specific output order seen in the example assertion.\n            new_combination = [item] + existing_combination\n            newly_formed_combinations.append(new_combination)\n        # Adds all newly formed combinations to the main list of all combinations.\n        all_combinations.extend(newly_formed_combinations)\n\n    return all_combinations"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray in the given list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    min_so_far = arr[0]\n    overall_max_product = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        num = arr[i]\n\n        # store the current max_so_far before it's updated for current num\n        temp_max_so_far = max_so_far\n\n        max_so_far = max(num, temp_max_so_far * num, min_so_far * num)\n        min_so_far = min(num, temp_max_so_far * num, min_so_far * num)\n\n        overall_max_product = max(overall_max_product, max_so_far)\n\n    return overall_max_product"}
