{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Odd_Pair(values, aux):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs of integers from 'values' whose bitwise XOR is odd.\n    The 'aux' parameter is ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_pair_count = 0\n    n = len(values)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            xor_val = values[i] ^ values[j]\n            if xor_val & 1 == 1:  # Check if the least significant bit is 1, indicating an odd number\n                odd_pair_count += 1\n    return odd_pair_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "def digit_distance_nums(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of absolute per-digit differences between two integers.\n    The shorter number is padded with leading zeros for alignment.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_a = str(abs(a))\n    s_b = str(abs(b))\n\n    max_len = max(len(s_a), len(s_b))\n\n    s_a = s_a.zfill(max_len)\n    s_b = s_b.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_diff = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit_a = int(s_a[i])\n        digit_b = int(s_b[i])\n        total_diff += abs(digit_a - digit_b)\n\n    return total_diff"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum(list, length):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest contiguous sublist in the given list.\n    Uses Kadane's algorithm for O(n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list:\n        return 0\n\n    max_ending_here = max_so_far = list[0]\n    for num in list[1:]:\n        max_ending_here = max(num, max_ending_here + num)\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
