{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "def two_unique_nums(input_list: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a list of integers that appear exactly once in the input list,\n    preserving their original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    from typing import List\n\n    # First pass: count occurrences of each number\n    counts = {}\n    for num in input_list:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    # Second pass: build the result list with numbers that occurred exactly once\n    result = []\n    for num in input_list:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n\n    return result"}
