{"task_id": "Mbpp/592", "solution": "def sum_Of_product(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of products of consecutive binomial coefficients C(n,k) * C(n,k+1).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0 # The sum is empty if n=0\n\n    # C(n, k) = C(n, k-1) * (n - k + 1) / k\n    # We can optimize the calculation of binomial coefficients iteratively.\n    # The sum is Sum[C(n,k) * C(n,k+1) for k from 0 to n-1]\n\n    current_binomial_coeff = 1  # C(n, 0)\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    for k in range(n):\n        next_binomial_coeff = current_binomial_coeff * (n - k) // (k + 1)\n        total_sum += current_binomial_coeff * next_binomial_coeff\n        current_binomial_coeff = next_binomial_coeff\n\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "def diff_even_odd(numbers: list) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the difference between the first even and first odd number in a list.\n    Returns (first even - first odd), or None if either parity is missing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list must contain at least one integer.\")\n\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if first_even is None and num % 2 == 0:\n            first_even = num\n        elif first_odd is None and num % 2 != 0:\n            first_odd = num\n\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n\n    if first_even is None or first_odd is None:\n        return None\n\n    return first_even - first_odd"}
