{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the nth Bell number using dynamic programming.\n    Raises ValueError if n is negative or not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize Bell triangle\n    bell = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # First row and first element of each row\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # First element of current row is last element of previous row\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i - 1][i - 1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Fill the remaining elements using the recurrence relation\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i - 1][j - 1] + bell[i][j - 1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row\n    return bell[n][0]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "def max_of_nth(matrix, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum value in the n-th column of a matrix.\n    Raises ValueError for an empty matrix, invalid column index, or inconsistent row lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        raise ValueError(\"Matrix cannot be empty.\")\n\n    num_cols = len(matrix[0])\n    if num_cols == 0 and n == 0:\n        # Handle case like [[]] for n=0\n        raise ValueError(\"Matrix has empty rows and column index 0 is invalid.\")\n    elif num_cols == 0:\n        # If first row is empty, no columns exist.\n        raise ValueError(\"Matrix rows cannot be empty.\")\n\n    if not (0 <= n < num_cols):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Column index {n} is out of bounds for a matrix with {num_cols} columns.\")\n\n    max_value = matrix[0][n]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(matrix)):\n        row = matrix[i]\n        if len(row) != num_cols:\n            raise ValueError(\"All rows in the matrix must have the same number of columns.\")\n        \n        current_value = row[n]\n        if current_value > max_value:\n            max_value = current_value\n\n    return max_value"}
