{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average cost of a path from the top-left to the bottom-right cell\n    of a square matrix, moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(matrix)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0.0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the maximum sum of costs to reach cell (i, j)\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Base case: starting cell\n    dp[0][0] = matrix[0][0]\n\n    # Fill first row (can only come from the left)\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][j] = matrix[0][j] + dp[0][j-1]\n\n    # Fill first column (can only come from above)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        dp[i][0] = matrix[i][0] + dp[i-1][0]\n\n    # Fill the rest of the DP table\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(1, n):\n            dp[i][j] = matrix[i][j] + max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    # The total number of cells in any valid path is always 2*N - 1\n    num_cells = 2 * n - 1\n    \n    # Calculate the maximum average\n    max_total_cost = dp[n-1][n-1]\n    return max_total_cost / num_cells"}
