{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "def left_insertion(list_obj, value):\n    \"\"\"Locates the left insertion point for a value in a sorted list using binary search.\"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(list_obj)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if list_obj[mid] < value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the smallest index k such that the triangular number T_k\n    has exactly n decimal digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        # Calculate the triangular number T_k = k(k+1)/2\n        triangular_number_value = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        \n        # Calculate the number of digits of T_k\n        num_digits = len(str(triangular_number_value))\n        \n        if num_digits == n:\n            return k\n        k += 1"}
