{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by k positions, returning a new list.\n    Handles empty lists, single-element lists, and k values greater than list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate effective rotation amount\n    k_effective = k % n\n\n    # If k_effective is 0, no rotation is needed\n    if k_effective == 0:\n        return list(lst) # Return a copy as required for new list\n\n    # Slice and concatenate to perform the rotation\n    return lst[n - k_effective:] + lst[:n - k_effective]"}
