{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum difference between any two elements in a given array.\n\n    The input `n` is ignored as the array length can be determined directly.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:  # According to requirement FR-002, though modern Python handles len(arr) directly.\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array must contain at least two elements.\")\n\n    # Convert to list and validate element types.\n    # The requirement FR-007 states \"Accept Iterable\" and FR-003 for validation.\n    # We will convert to list to enable sorting and consistent indexing.\n    arr_list = []\n    for x in arr:\n        if not isinstance(x, int):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in the array must be integers.\")\n        arr_list.append(x)\n    \n    # Sort the array (O(n log n) complexity as per FR-005).\n    arr_list.sort()\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through adjacent elements to find the minimum difference.\n    # This is an efficient way after sorting to find the minimum difference (O(n)).\n    for i in range(len(arr_list) - 1):\n        diff = arr_list[i+1] - arr_list[i]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n\n    return min_diff\n```"}
