{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence in the right half\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    This function uses an arithmetic progression formula for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine the first odd number in the range [l, r]\n    start = l if l % 2 != 0 else l + 1\n    # Determine the last odd number in the range [l, r]\n    end = r if r % 2 != 0 else r - 1\n\n    # If the adjusted start is greater than the adjusted end, there are no odd numbers.\n    if start > end:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the count of odd numbers in the arithmetic progression.\n    count = ((end - start) // 2) + 1\n\n    # Calculate the sum using the arithmetic series formula: n/2 * (first_term + last_term).\n    total = count * (start + end) // 2\n    return total"}
